{"id":44882,"brand_id":228,"unique_id":"B46TNVL354tXk0hF","content_key":"/p/15years","identifies_id":228,"identifies_type":"Brand","title":"15 Years of Generosity","data":{"blocks":[{"col_1":[],"layout":"block_2","col_order":["col_1"],"spacer_top":{"max":128,"min":0,"val":0},"backgrounds":[{"url":"https://imagecdn.mightycause.com/eaf2380a-afec-4d4b-92b3-c9463e150230/","uuid":"eaf2380a-afec-4d4b-92b3-c9463e150230"}],"spacer_bottom":{"max":128,"min":0,"val":0},"spacer_mobile":true,"background_type":"image","background_color":null,"background_solid":null,"background_opacity":0},{"col_1":[{"max":128,"min":16,"val":16,"type":"spacer","uuid":"b57f8f3a-fd7a-492c-b336-13a1be28998f"},{"url":"https://imagecdn.mightycause.com/4460b448-d899-4dce-93be-5810ef4775b5/-/preview/","type":"image","uuid":"4460b448-d899-4dce-93be-5810ef4775b5","scale":"scale-100","width":1748,"height":1166,"content":"15years-of-generosity.jpg","new_tab":false,"alt_text":null,"link_url":null,"position":"center"}],"col_2":[{"max":128,"min":16,"val":16,"type":"spacer","uuid":"1b94742e-7cdd-498f-8013-4542ac8727b4"},{"type":"text","uuid":"343218b9-fa56-4ce6-aa5e-30f3a0c746fd","content":"\u003ch1 data-pasted=\"true\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThe Story of Give Miami Day:\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e15 Years of Generosity\u003c/h1\u003e\u003cp\u003eAs we mark 15 years of Give Miami Day, we sat down with the leaders, nonprofits, sponsors, and donors who started it all \u0026mdash; and who are steering Miami\u0026rsquo;s most generous day into its future. Fifteen years ago, research showed Miami was one of the least civically engaged communities in the country. Give Miami Day started as an idea to flip that script, and it\u0026rsquo;s been growing Miami\u0026rsquo;s culture of giving ever since.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003cspan style=\"color: rgb(106, 62, 189);\"\u003eWatch their stories below.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"}],"layout":"block_6","col_order":["col_1","col_2"],"spacer_top":{"max":128,"min":0,"val":32},"backgrounds":[],"spacer_bottom":{"max":128,"min":0,"val":32},"spacer_mobile":true,"background_type":"color","background_color":null,"background_solid":null,"background_opacity":0},{"col_1":[{"src":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VqzaGWnf7wE","type":"video","uuid":"b2b15a5f-039f-466d-9135-f195e513eba3","scale":"scale-100","position":"center"},{"type":"text","uuid":"35b1fe0b-10e4-42b4-9680-faffb1a807bf","content":"\u003ch2\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003cspan style=\"color: rgb(106, 62, 189);\"\u003eThen \u0026amp; Now\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cp\u003eFifteen years ago, a handful of Miamians dreamed big for this city. Watch as they reflect on how that idea became Miami\u0026rsquo;s biggest day of giving \u0026mdash; and what\u0026rsquo;s still ahead.\u003c/p\u003e"},{"type":"text","uuid":"3cc9371f-d8d0-42f2-95fe-2abbee6cb8fa","content":"\u003ch3 data-pasted=\"true\"\u003e\u003cem\u003e\u003cspan style=\"font-size: 21px;\"\u003e\u0026ldquo;Even I, with my outsized expectations for this, had no idea that we could get this far, this fast.\u0026rdquo;\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/h3\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e- Alberto Ibarg\u0026uuml;en, former CEO and President, John S. and James L. Knight Foundation\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"}],"col_2":[{"src":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YHzjwO1-czQ","type":"video","uuid":"9ab62f34-3533-4e4f-a544-0234da388ebf","scale":"scale-100","position":"center"},{"type":"text","uuid":"794d3d36-84f9-4106-bb9f-07ffbb48d849","content":"\u003ch2\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003cspan style=\"color: rgb(106, 62, 189);\"\u003eThe Nonprofit Perspective\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cp\u003eFrom crisis response to cultural preservation, nonprofits show up for Miami every single day. Watch the leaders behind that work describe what Give Miami Day means to them.\u003c/p\u003e"},{"type":"text","uuid":"a92f6099-3c21-4e60-9f7e-c4b0c1fb6833","content":"\u003ch3 data-pasted=\"true\"\u003e\u003cem\u003e\u003cspan style=\"font-size: 21px;\"\u003e\u0026ldquo;When we meet a family that is in crisis, we can take some of that money and support them in a way that is immediate and that is real and that is impactful.\u0026rdquo;\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/h3\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e- Thamara Labrousse, Executive Director, Sant La Haitian Neighborhood Center\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"}],"layout":"block_3","col_order":["col_1","col_2"],"spacer_top":{"max":128,"min":0,"val":32},"backgrounds":[],"spacer_bottom":{"max":128,"min":0,"val":32},"spacer_mobile":true,"background_type":"color","background_color":null,"background_solid":null,"background_opacity":0},{"col_1":[{"max":128,"min":16,"val":16,"type":"spacer","uuid":"d85d5fab-bddd-4f31-a060-3390d5f3b037"},{"src":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bdBoiwKx_DQ","type":"video","uuid":"c1d2fcba-845b-4f50-8d6c-2853819a275e","scale":"scale-100","position":"center"}],"col_2":[{"max":128,"min":16,"val":16,"type":"spacer","uuid":"b6719dd7-a31a-4115-af4d-535d8e0e1991"},{"type":"text","uuid":"94146cf5-0d8f-4d36-af5f-736c613a6f4e","content":"\u003ch2\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003cspan style=\"color: rgb(106, 62, 189);\"\u003eThe Backbone Perspective\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan style=\"color: rgb(106, 62, 189);\"\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cp data-pasted=\"true\"\u003eBehind every Give Miami Day gift is a someone investing in this city\u0026rsquo;s future. Hear from the sponsors who see themselves not only as funders, but as partners together with us.\u003c/p\u003e"},{"type":"text","uuid":"6ee1b5d3-4e3d-43da-a3b1-e678bea7aae1","content":"\u003ch3 data-pasted=\"true\"\u003e\u003cem\u003e\u0026ldquo;Give Miami Day is really this testament to the donors in our community. Anyone can be a philanthropist. Everyone can make a difference.\u0026rdquo;\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/h3\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e- Jennifer Stearns Buttrick, Director of Pro Bono and Community Involvement, Stearns Weaver Miller\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"}],"layout":"block_3","col_order":["col_1","col_2"],"spacer_top":{"max":128,"min":0,"val":32},"backgrounds":[],"spacer_bottom":{"max":128,"min":0,"val":32},"spacer_mobile":true,"background_type":"color","background_color":null,"background_solid":"#f5f5f5","background_opacity":0},{"col_1":[{"max":128,"min":16,"val":16,"type":"spacer","uuid":"7cb10438-5c41-4dec-9739-e920a543197b"},{"type":"text","uuid":"4b5d6921-42b6-4a37-95e9-7527fe5f514f","content":"\u003cdiv style=\"text-align: center;\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003ch2 style=\"text-align: center;\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003cspan style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"\u003eHow will you celebrate 15 Years of Generosity?\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/h2\u003e"},[{"url":"https://www.givemiamiday.org/p/give","fill":true,"size":"large","type":"button","uuid":"d5541a55-1b23-45f3-8860-fa57941566f8","color":"#6a3ebd","shape":"rectangle","invert":true,"content":"Plan Your Giving Celebration","new_tab":false,"position":"center"}]],"layout":"block_1","col_order":["col_1"],"spacer_top":{"max":128,"min":0,"val":32},"backgrounds":[{"url":"https://imagecdn.mightycause.com/023121ed-416c-45fc-82dc-d1bf32f014d6/","uuid":"023121ed-416c-45fc-82dc-d1bf32f014d6"}],"spacer_bottom":{"max":128,"min":0,"val":32},"spacer_mobile":true,"background_type":"color","background_color":null,"background_solid":"#6a3ebd","background_opacity":0}],"header":{"config":{"hide":false,"gradient":true,"textStyle":"light"}}},"version":1,"published_at":"2026-11-03T15:00:46.000-05:00","deleted_at":null,"redirect_type":null,"redirect_url":null,"updated_at":"2026-11-03T15:00:46.000-05:00","created_at":"2026-11-02T14:57:02.000-05:00","internal_ref_title":"15 Years","milestone_id":null,"giving_event_id":747,"is_fallback":false,"metadata_computed":{"description":"","og_title":"15 Years of Generosity","og_description":null,"og